{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Which he does for the people.</b> These trouble those, and they stand and wait all day long — when will they come to judgment before him?" "<b>Why do you sit alone.</b> He did not rebuke him for the fact that he sat while they stood, for that is indeed how judgment is: the judge sits and the litigants stand, as it is written: ועמדו שני האנשים אשר להם הריב. Nor was it for Jethro to rebuke a man as great as Moses, since Aaron, who was older than Moses by three years, said to him: בי אדוני. Rather, this is what it says: what is your thinking, to sit and judge alone? You should have assembled with you many sages to judge with you, to lighten the burden upon you, and not sit in judgment alone. And Moses thought in his heart that Jethro was asking him why they were standing about him, and to this he answered him: כי יבא אלי העם etc." "<b>From morning until evening.</b> Even though you sit in judgment the entire day, you alone cannot manage to judge them all."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:34.901088702Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}